            <div xml:id="d835">

                <pb facs="0841" n="837" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg837"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51 Salt Funds/229: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Peck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-06-04T10:00:00+07:00">June 4, 1939—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 4—5 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>359. My 198, March 22, 3 p.m. Lockhart has been negotiating with the Chinese
                    authorities concerned and has now handed to the Embassy a memorandum dated May
                    26 describing the way in which, contrary to various undertakings given by them,
                    the Chinese have curtailed the authority of the foreign officials of the Salt
                    Administration and asserting that this action creates doubt in regard to the
                    value of the salt revenue as dependable security for American and other
                    obligations. The writer inquires whether the Embassy might not be authorized to
                    support his position with a view to the protection of American interests
                    involved. Text of the memorandum is going forward by air mail.<anchor n="81"
                        xml:id="d835-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Writer informs me that he described the situation to the British Ambassador and
                    the latter indicated willingness to join in representations to the Chinese
                    Government. I infer it is the writer’s intention to approach the French
                    Ambassador when he arrives in Chungking about June 10.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping, Shanghai.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peck</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
